# Unified KB deny-list (INI format) — TEMPLATE.
# Copy to ./root/.exclude.conf (gitignored) and edit with your trees' paths.
# LOCAL ONLY: ./root/.exclude.conf may hold Drive file paths (business-sensitive,
# PII) and is deliberately NOT committed — keep this template generic.
#
# ONE file, read by BOTH index stages with the SAME pattern semantics:
#   - gdrive-sync  : the rclone download stage (./root/gdrive from the gdrive
#                    remote) converts the active sections to rclone --exclude-from.
#   - api-gateway  : the index walk stage (POST /index?dir=<name>) applies the
#                    active sections as a post-walk filter before the manifest.
#
# [section] header = a path RELATIVE to ./root/ (the source root). Examples:
#   [*]              special section: a GLOBAL deny-list. Its patterns apply to
#                    EVERY KB (every top-level ./root/ subdir). Use for content
#                    types you never want indexed in any KB (e.g. *.py, *.json).
#                    A type denied in [*] CANNOT be un-denied for a single KB —
#                    the deny-list is additive on top of the global allow-list.
#   [<kb>]           one KB: patterns apply only to ./root/<kb>/ (a top-level
#                    subdir). Example: [my-docs].
#   [<kb>/<sub>]     a sub-tree of one KB: patterns apply only to files under
#                    ./root/<kb>/<sub>/. Example: [gdrive/Team Meetings].
#
# Section selection for a walk of dir=<D>: [*]  +  every section S where
#   S == D  or  D startswith S+"/"  (ancestors)  or  S startswith D+"/"  (descendants).
# So dir=gdrive selects [*], [gdrive], [gdrive/Team Meetings], etc. — NOT [my-docs].
#
# Patterns are rclone-native (shared by both stages):
#   no "/"  -> matches the basename at ANY depth (file.pdf, *.tmp, or a lone "*"
#              = every file in the section);
#   "/"     -> ANCHORS at the section root: a full path relative to the section.
#              Example: in [gdrive/Team Meetings], /Weekly*.pdf anchors at
#              ./root/gdrive/Team Meetings/ (NOT every drive's /Weekly*.pdf).
#   "/" elsewhere (no leading "/") -> a path pattern, FULL-matched against the
#              path relative to the section (rclone-native). "*" does not cross
#              "/", so "*/x.pdf" matches a one-level "<seg>/x.pdf" only, NOT a
#              deeper "a/b/x.pdf". Use "**/x.pdf" to cross directory boundaries,
#              or a bare basename "x.pdf" to match it at ANY depth.
#   *       -> matches any run of chars EXCEPT "/" (does NOT cross a "/");
#   **      -> matches across "/" (crosses directory boundaries);
#   ?       -> matches a single char except "/".
#
# LEAF-ONLY ANCHORED PATTERNS: a "/"-anchored pattern is allowed ONLY in a LEAF
# section (a section with no deeper section under it). A non-leaf section ([*],
# [gdrive]) anchors at different roots for the rclone download stage vs the
# gateway index stage, so an anchored pattern there is ambiguous and is REJECTED
# (fail-closed) by both stages. Put anchored patterns in a leaf section such as
# [gdrive/<drive>] or [<kb>].
#
# [*] below is the GLOBAL deny-list (kept verbatim from the pre-./root layout):
# these types are NOT indexed in ANY KB. Per-KB sections below are ADDITIVE
# further-denies (they can only exclude more, never re-include a [*]-denied type).

[*]
*.tmp
*.pyc
*.py
*.csv
# gdrive-meta sidecars: local-only, protected from sync deletion + never downloaded.
# *.meta (YAML) here; *.meta.json (JSON, the gateway-read copy) is covered by *.json
# below AND by the gateway's hardcoded sidecar skip (an invariant, not just config).
*.meta
*.json
*.s
*.c
*.h
*.inc
*.cfg

# One KB (a top-level ./root/ subdir). Additive further-denies for that KB only.
[my-docs]
*.aux
*.log
*.toc

# A sub-tree of the gdrive KB (a descendant section; leaf, so anchored patterns OK).
[gdrive/Team Meetings]
/Weekly*.pdf